    "q-161670": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161670",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "What is the distance between the points $(-1,5)$  and $(3,5)?$",
      "worked_solution": "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14179134/assets/74dfce8c8444a841f9f742d70204d82b22157bf5b955bb2691eb0cdefe62fb75.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $4$ units, so the distance equals $4.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14179134/assets/4df0d2515a43236634f934879d6a4d8926cc09163f79216ce288e07e2ba28e72.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14179134/assets/aaf091301a2b004e80bef49a2893eed00f0a28693d8799ee366ed47425869a9c.png)\n\nThe point $(-1,5)$ is at a distance of $1$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(3,5)$ is at a distance of $3$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $1+3=4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
